# One word in each pair already carries the other. `refer back` is
# left out, because recursion prose needs it (`a value that refers
# back to itself`), and so are `write down` and `empty space`, which
# name a physical act and a layout region. `continue on` counts only
# before `to` (`continues on to the next entry`), because a CI step
# continues on error.
#
# Each verb carries its inflections. `$merge` expands to merge,
# merges, merged, and merging through Harper's dictionary. `return`,
# `reply`, and `plan` list their forms by hand, because the dictionary
# gives no past tense for them.
#
# `still remain` sits in the Recommended rule of the same name.
expr main [(each and every), (first and foremost), (any and all), (various different), (end result), (final outcome), (advance planning), (past history), (free gift), (added bonus), (basic fundamentals), (close proximity), (exact same), (future plans), (new innovation), (past experience), (period of time), (sum total), (true fact), (unexpected surprise), (absolutely essential), (brief summary), (mutual cooperation), (unintentional mistake), (general consensus), (final end), (actual fact), (the reason is because), (reason why), (may possibly), (might possibly), (could possibly), (can potentially), (could potentially), (may potentially), (might potentially), (completely finished), (fully complete), (fully completed), (totally complete), (entirely complete), (absolutely necessary), (necessary requirement), (required prerequisite), (prerequisite requirement), (advance warning), (advance notice), (personal opinion), (own personal), (small in size), (large in size), (few in number), (many in number), (twelve noon), (twelve midnight), (temporary reprieve), (time period), (unfilled vacancy), (usual custom), ([$merge, $combine, $collaborate, $link, $join] together), ([return, returns, returned, returning, reply, replies, replied, replying, $revert] back), ($repeat again), (completely $eliminate), ($continue on to), ($ask the question), ([plan, plans, planned, planning] ahead), ($protest against), ($postpone until later)]
let message "Redundant pair. One of the two words carries the meaning."
let description "Flags word pairs where one word already includes the other."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "A value that refers back to itself never finishes the walk."
allows "Write down the recovery code before closing the dialog."
allows "The gutter fills the empty space to the left of the text."
allows "The step continues on error."
